---
import Base from '../layouts/Base.astro';
---

<Base
  title="Quant explainer"
  description="Q3 through Q8, Unsloth UD dynamic GGUFs, BF16, KV cache types, and why Q1/Q2 stay off this site. Links to the calculator."
>
  <main id="main" class="mx-auto max-w-3xl px-4 py-10 sm:px-6">
    <p class="font-mono text-[0.72rem] uppercase tracking-[0.18em] text-accent">Weights</p>
    <h1 class="mt-3 font-serif text-4xl tracking-tight sm:text-5xl">Quants, without folklore</h1>
    <p class="mt-4 text-lg leading-relaxed text-muted">
      A quant is a stored-weight encoding. Lower bits shrink the file and usually cost quality.
      This site lists <strong class="text-ink">Q3 through BF16</strong>. Q3 rows are estimates
      or community results unless a tested badge says otherwise. Our local-desktop measurements stay
      Q4 and above. The
      <a class="underline decoration-accent/40 underline-offset-2" href="/calculator">calculator</a>
      estimates VRAM from these encodings.
    </p>

    <section class="mt-10">
      <h2 class="font-serif text-3xl">Q3 through Q8 (llama.cpp family)</h2>
      <p class="mt-3 leading-relaxed text-muted">
        Nominal bits-per-weight used by the calculator (llama.cpp-family labels, not measured entropy):
      </p>
      <div class="mt-4 overflow-x-auto">
        <table class="min-w-[28rem] w-full text-left text-sm">
          <thead>
            <tr class="border-b border-line text-faint">
              <th class="py-2 pr-3 font-mono text-[0.68rem] uppercase tracking-[0.12em]">Quant</th>
              <th class="py-2 pr-3 font-mono text-[0.68rem] uppercase tracking-[0.12em]">Nominal bpw</th>
              <th class="py-2 font-mono text-[0.68rem] uppercase tracking-[0.12em]">House note</th>
            </tr>
          </thead>
          <tbody>
            <tr class="border-b border-line/70"><td class="py-2 pr-3">Q3_K_S</td><td class="py-2 pr-3 font-mono">3.50</td><td class="py-2 text-muted">Estimate / community. 35B listing: Unsloth UD-Q3_K_S 15.4 GB.</td></tr>
            <tr class="border-b border-line/70"><td class="py-2 pr-3">Q3_K_M</td><td class="py-2 pr-3 font-mono">3.91</td><td class="py-2 text-muted">Estimate / community. 35B listing: Unsloth UD-Q3_K_M 16.6 GB.</td></tr>
            <tr class="border-b border-line/70"><td class="py-2 pr-3">UD-Q3_K_XL</td><td class="py-2 pr-3 font-mono">3.91</td><td class="py-2 text-muted">Estimate / community. 35B listing: Unsloth UD-Q3_K_XL 16.8 GB.</td></tr>
            <tr class="border-b border-line/70"><td class="py-2 pr-3">IQ3 / UD-IQ3_S</td><td class="py-2 pr-3 font-mono">3.44</td><td class="py-2 text-muted">Estimate / community, only where the repo lists IQ3. 35B listing: Unsloth UD-IQ3_S 13.7 GB.</td></tr>
            <tr class="border-b border-line/70"><td class="py-2 pr-3">Q4_K_M</td><td class="py-2 pr-3 font-mono">4.85</td><td class="py-2 text-muted">Measured on our rig for the 35B sibling. Prefer Q5 when it fits.</td></tr>
            <tr class="border-b border-line/70"><td class="py-2 pr-3">Q5_K_M / UD-Q5_K_XL</td><td class="py-2 pr-3 font-mono">5.69</td><td class="py-2 text-muted">Daily-driver family. Prefer Q5 over Q4.</td></tr>
            <tr class="border-b border-line/70"><td class="py-2 pr-3">Q6_K / UD-Q6_K_XL</td><td class="py-2 pr-3 font-mono">6.56</td><td class="py-2 text-muted">Flash agent family on our rig.</td></tr>
            <tr class="border-b border-line/70"><td class="py-2 pr-3">Q8_0</td><td class="py-2 pr-3 font-mono">8.5</td><td class="py-2 text-muted">Near-lossless GGUF; heavy.</td></tr>
            <tr class="border-b border-line/70"><td class="py-2 pr-3">BF16</td><td class="py-2 pr-3 font-mono">16</td><td class="py-2 text-muted">Unquantized. Rarely a home fit.</td></tr>
          </tbody>
        </table>
      </div>
      <p class="mt-3 text-sm text-faint">
        File sizes for the 35B Q3/Q5 rows come from
        <a class="underline decoration-accent/40 underline-offset-2" href="https://huggingface.co/unsloth/Qwen3.6-35B-A3B-GGUF/tree/main">unsloth/Qwen3.6-35B-A3B-GGUF</a>
        (UD-Q5_K_XL 26.6 GB). Flash:
        <a class="underline decoration-accent/40 underline-offset-2" href="https://huggingface.co/unsloth/Qwen3.8-Flash-Next-GGUF">unsloth/Qwen3.8-Flash-Next-GGUF</a>
        (UD-Q6_K_XL folder ~169 GB; UD-Q3_K_XL folder ~90 GB / LFS 89.99 GB; UD-IQ3_XXS LFS 81.96 GB). Quality deltas for Q3 are not measured on local-desktop.
      </p>
    </section>

    <section class="mt-10">
      <h2 class="font-serif text-3xl">Unsloth UD dynamic quants</h2>
      <p class="mt-3 leading-relaxed text-muted">
        Unsloth’s UD (dynamic) GGUFs mix higher-precision tensors into a named bucket so important
        layers stay closer to the original. We do not invent a quality delta. When the publisher
        lists a file size, the calculator uses that size instead of <code class="text-ink">params × bpw</code>.
        Prefer the UD-Q5_K_XL / UD-Q6_K_XL files we name on <a class="underline decoration-accent/40 underline-offset-2" href="/stacks">/stacks</a>
        when you want the daily-driver or Flash path. UD-Q3_K_XL is the Q3 size step on the same card.
      </p>
    </section>

    <section class="mt-10">
      <h2 class="font-serif text-3xl">KV cache types</h2>
      <p class="mt-3 leading-relaxed text-muted">
        Weights are one allocation. Context is another. The calculator’s KV estimate is
        <code class="text-ink">2 × kv_layers × kv_heads × head_dim × context × bytes</code>.
        Hybrid Qwen cards (3.6 / 3.8 Flash) only grow KV on full-attention layers — that count
        comes from the public model card, not from our tape measure.
      </p>
      <ul class="mt-4 list-disc space-y-2 pl-5 text-muted">
        <li><strong class="text-ink">f16</strong> — 2 bytes. Daily driver on our rig.</li>
        <li><strong class="text-ink">q8_0</strong> — 1 byte. Smaller KV; quality trade is not measured here.</li>
        <li><strong class="text-ink">q4_0</strong> — 0.5 bytes. Last KV lever before you cut context. This is a KV type, not a weight quant.</li>
      </ul>
    </section>

    <section class="mt-10">
      <h2 class="font-serif text-3xl">Q1 and Q2 stay off</h2>
      <p class="mt-3 leading-relaxed text-muted">
        Q1, Q2, IQ1, and IQ2 (including draft / MTP heads) stay off this site. They exist in
        the GGUF ecosystem. Q3 is listed with a publisher size when we have one, and labeled
        estimate or community unless we measured it. Prefer Q5 over Q4 when the file still fits.
      </p>
    </section>

    <p class="mt-10">
      <a class="btn-primary" href="/calculator">Open the Quant + Hardware Calculator</a>
    </p>
  </main>
</Base>
